## Task 2 — Analytics API routes
Create all five routes using createClient directly with env vars.
Never import from @/lib/supabase.

Create app/api/analytics/top-searches/route.ts:
- GET handler
- const supabase = createClient(
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!
  )
- calls supabase.rpc('analytics_top_searches')
- returns NextResponse.json({ data })
- on error: console.error and return { data: null } with status 500

Create app/api/analytics/top-assets/route.ts:
- Same pattern, calls supabase.rpc('analytics_top_assets')
- returns { data: Array<{ ticker, company_name, count }> }

Create app/api/analytics/search-volume/route.ts:
- Same pattern, calls supabase.rpc('analytics_search_volume')
- returns { data: Array<{ date, count }> }

Create app/api/analytics/trending/route.ts:
- Same pattern, calls supabase.rpc('analytics_trending')
- returns { data: Array<{ query, count }> }

Create app/api/analytics/watchlist-stats/route.ts:
- Same pattern, calls supabase.rpc('analytics_watchlist_stats')
- Transform rows into: 
  { watchlist: number, researching: number, invested: number, total: number }
- returns { data: { watchlist, researching, invested, total } }

